  "title": {
    "en": "How this site is built: a static blog on a homelab"
  },
  "description": {
    "en": "A headless CMS, a static Astro build, and nginx pods that keep serving even when the CMS is down. The reasoning and the trade-offs."
  },
  "content": {
    "en": {
      "root": {
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "version": 1,
        "children": [
          {
            "direction": "ltr",
            "format": "",
            "indent": 0,
            "version": 1,
            "children": [
              {
                "detail": 0,
                "format": 0,
                "mode": "normal",
                "style": "",
                "text": "This site is a ",
                "type": "text",
                "version": 1
              },
              {
                "detail": 0,
                "format": 1,
                "mode": "normal",
                "style": "",
                "text": "static",
                "type": "text",
                "version": 1
              },
              {
                "detail": 0,
                "format": 0,
                "mode": "normal",
                "style": "",
                "text": " Astro build. The words live in a headless CMS, but readers never touch it: they get plain files from ",
                "type": "text",
                "version": 1
              },
              {
                "detail": 0,
                "format": 16,
                "mode": "normal",
                "style": "",
                "text": "nginx",
                "type": "text",
                "version": 1
              },
              {
                "detail": 0,
                "format": 0,
                "mode": "normal",
                "style": "",
                "text": " (or from a mirror in object storage when the homelab is down).",
                "type": "text",
                "version": 1
              }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
          },
          {
            "direction": "ltr",
            "format": "",
            "indent": 0,
            "version": 1,
            "children": [
              {
                "detail": 0,
                "format": 0,
                "mode": "normal",
                "style": "",
                "text": "The shape of it",
                "type": "text",
                "version": 1
              }
            ],
            "type": "heading",
            "tag": "h2"
          },
          {
            "direction": "ltr",
            "format": "",
            "indent": 0,
            "version": 1,
            "children": [
              {
                "detail": 0,
                "format": 0,
                "mode": "normal",
                "style": "",
                "text": "Publishing in the CMS triggers a build. The build produces a ",
                "type": "text",
                "version": 1
              },
              {
                "detail": 0,
                "format": 16,
                "mode": "normal",
                "style": "",
                "text": "dist/",
                "type": "text",
                "version": 1
              },
              {
                "detail": 0,
                "format": 0,
                "mode": "normal",
                "style": "",
                "text": " folder, uploads it as a numbered release, and moves a pointer. The pods notice the new pointer and swap their content without a rollout.",
                "type": "text",
                "version": 1
              }
            ],
            "type": "paragraph"
          },
          {
            "fields": {
              "id": "fx0001",
              "blockName": "",
              "blockType": "diagram",
              "kind": "d2",
              "source": "direction: right\nauthor: You { shape: person }\ncms: Payload CMS\nci: GitHub Actions\nr2: Object storage { shape: cylinder }\npods: nginx pods\nauthor -> cms: publish\ncms -> ci: dispatch\nci -> r2: upload release\npods -> r2: poll LATEST"
            },
            "format": "",
            "type": "block",
            "version": 2
          },
          {
            "direction": "ltr",
            "format": "",
            "indent": 0,
            "version": 1,
            "children": [
              {
                "detail": 0,
                "format": 0,
                "mode": "normal",
                "style": "",
                "text": "How releases are laid out:",
